vice that offers a combination of quantum and classical computation resources and advanced algorithms to solve problems of enterprise scale; and D-Wave Launch, a phased approach to identify and build in-production quantum hybrid applications, including training sessions and quantum computing access. In addition, the company offers D-Wave Advantage annealing quantum computing systems; and Ocean developer tools. Its quantum solutions are used in allocation, resource scheduling, factory scheduling, vehicle routing, logistics optimization, drug discovery, industrial construction design, portfolio optimization and maintenance, repair, and overhaul optimization. The company has a collaboration with the University of Arkansas to establish leadership, education, and independent research focused on the application of quantum computing to supply chain management across retail, transportation, and national defense. D-Wave Quantum Inc. was founded in 1999 and is based in Palo Alto, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Alan E. Baratz Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 70 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 382 people. Revenue per employee of $64K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 51%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $59K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["D-Wave Quantum Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $3.6B market cap on $25M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +51% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -1316% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 61% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $76M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -25.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 1.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 92% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 415% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 205% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"QBTS Stock Down 45% Since August: The $40.7M Backlog Behind the Rebound Case","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/qbts-stock-down-45-since-133650270.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577010.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"QBTS INVESTOR DEADLINE: D-Wave Quantum Inc. Investors with Substantial Losses May Seek to Lead Class Action Lawsuit Before December 15, 2026 Deadline","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/qbts-investor-deadline-d-wave-quantum-inc-investors-with-substantial-losses-may-seek-to-lead-class-action-lawsuit-before-december-15-2026-deadline-302937634.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794524400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"What Does D-Wave Quantum, Inc.'s 9.51% Stock Drop Mean for Investors? The Law Offices of Howard G. Smith Outlines Securities Fraud Class Action Lead Plaintiff Deadline","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/what-does-d-wave-quantum-incs-9-51-stock-drop-mean-for-investors-the-law-offices-of-howard-g-smith-outlines-securities-fraud-class-action-lead-plaintiff-deadline-302938562.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794594600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.527,"tier":1,"